reating the  new displacements on the new model there  are several hurdles to overcome  one we cannot just grab the  displacements and shove them onto a  different model because it can  potentially look different  have different curvatures and sizes the  solution to this would be capturing the  statistical properties of the surface  details and use this information to  synthesize new ones on the target model  note that we cannot just perform this  texture synthesis in 2d like we do for  images because as we project the result  to a 3d model it introduces severe  distortions to the displacement patterns  it is a bit like putting a rubber  blanket onto a complicated object  different regions of the blanket will be  distorted differently make sure to have  a look at the paper where the authors  present quite a few more results and of  course the intricacies of this technique  are also described in detail I hope some  public implementations of this method  will appear soon I would be quite  excited to use this right away and I am  sure there are many artists who would  love to create these wonderfully  detailed models for the animated films  and computer games of the future in the  meantime we have a completely overhauled  software and hardware pipeline to create  these videos we have written down our  joyful and perilous story of it on  patreon if you are interested in looking  a bit behind the curtain as to how these  episodes are made make sure to have a  look it is available in the video  description thanks for watching and for  your generous support now see you next  time  [Music]
 

